  <section id="cxp-rules-overview">
    <h2>1. Overview</h2>
    <p class="lead">Experience points remain a single resource. Only XP spent on <strong>permanent character development</strong> advances a character toward the next tier.</p>
    <div class="cxp-rules-grid">
      <article class="cxp-rules-card">
        <h3>Immediate XP</h3>
        <p>XP spent to affect the current situation: rerolls, intrusions, insights, and temporary advantages. It does <strong>not</strong> create Development Progress.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="cxp-rules-card">
        <h3>Development XP</h3>
        <p>XP spent on a lasting improvement: skills, abilities, Pool increases, assets, and similar changes. It creates Development Progress.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="cxp-rules-rule"><strong>Core Rule.</strong> When a character spends XP on a qualifying permanent development purchase, add the full XP cost to that character's lifetime Development Progress.</div>
    <div class="cxp-rules-formula">Development Progress Gained = XP Spent on Qualifying Permanent Development</div>
    <p>There is no requirement to purchase four separate advancement categories. A character may buy as many permitted permanent advancements as they wish.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="cxp-rules-progress">
    <h2>2. Development Progress and Tiers</h2>
    <p>Development Progress is cumulative and never resets. When a character reaches a threshold, they immediately gain that tier. Progress beyond a threshold remains recorded and contributes to the next tier.</p>
    <table>
      <caption>Tier thresholds</caption>
      <thead><tr><th>New Tier</th><th>Total Progress Required</th><th>Additional Progress Required</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Tier 2</td><td>24</td><td>24</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Tier 3</td><td>60</td><td>36</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Tier 4</td><td>112</td><td>52</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Tier 5</td><td>184</td><td>72</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Tier 6</td><td>280</td><td>96</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <div class="cxp-rules-rule"><strong>Result.</strong> Characters grow continuously, but each later tier demands considerably more investment. High-tier characters are exceptional because their progress represents a long history of permanent development.</div>
  </section>

